        "original_id": "bd756064-5120-5d6a-9078-e8a83cdf0396",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Morrie Schwartz, Mitch Albom, Thomas Rickman, Mick Jackson, Jack Lemmon, Hank Azaria\n- Works: Tuesdays with Morrie, Detroit Free Press\n- Topics: living funerals, TV film adaptations\n\nFacts:\n- Morrie Schwartz had a well-known living funeral that was documented in the book and film \"Tuesdays with Morrie.\"\n- Mitch Albom, a Detroit Free Press sports columnist, was one of the central figures in \"Tuesdays with Morrie.\"\n- Thomas Rickman later adapted \"Tuesdays with Morrie\" into a television film of the same name.\n- Mick Jackson directed the \"Tuesdays with Morrie\" TV movie.\n- The television film \"Tuesdays with Morrie\" aired on December 5, 1999.\n- Jack Lemmon and Hank Azaria starred in the 1999 TV movie \"Tuesdays with Morrie.\"",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "b8ba8a09-878a-574c-86bb-0949f5c246b7",
        "text": "Page: Living funeral. Sentence: One of the more famous living funerals was that for Morrie Schwartz which was documented in both the book and film \"Tuesdays with Morrie\" and feature \"Detroit Free Press\" sports columnist Mitch Albom as one of the central characters.\nPage: Tuesdays with Morrie. Sentence: The story was later recreated by Thomas Rickman into a TV movie of the same name directed by Mick Jackson, which aired on December 5, 1999 and starred Jack Lemmon and Hank Azaria.",
